        "title": "Material Culture and the History of Things",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Material culture history studies the physical objects, artifacts, environments, and substances\nthat humans make, use, and inhabit. Things are not just passive products of society — they shape\nhuman practice, embody social relations, and carry meanings. The \"material turn\" in the 1990s-2000s\nbrought objects back to the center of historical analysis."
